{{!--
    The radio group of one MCP access section (instance management or email access), rendered
    identically by the OAuth consent prompt, the MCP config page's generator and the token form
    so the three cannot drift on what each level promises. The options come from MCP_SECTIONS
    (lib/token-permission-view.js), which also carries the pair list each level mints.
    Params:
      section     - the section object from MCP_SECTIONS (required)
      name        - input name shared by the radio group (required; the pages name it
                    <prefix><section key>, which is what static/js/ui.js reads back)
      idPrefix    - per-page prefix for the input ids; ids are <idPrefix>_<level> (required)
      selected    - the selected level (required)
      includeNone - true to offer the section's decline option first (the consent prompt and the
                    generator; the token form declines a section by leaving its scope unticked)
--}}
{{#if includeNone}}
{{> ui/radio id=(concat idPrefix "_none") name=name value="none" label=section.none.label selected=selected hint=section.none.hint}}
{{/if}}
{{#each section.levels}}
{{> ui/radio id=(concat ../idPrefix "_" value) name=../name value=value label=label selected=../selected hint=hint}}
{{/each}}
